      "sourceLink": null,
      "spam": false,
      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "bump... still valid points almost 10 years later. ;)\n\nWhen do we get a weighted / adjusted ranking system ...\n\ninstead of adding layers on top of other defunct and obsolete layers of calculation (group instance performance gating *cough* *cough* )\n\nAlso as mentionned in other canny too: \n\nfor GPU / VRAM bound characteristics, it should be based onto the real PC specs of the end user. \n\nNot targetted randomly for all for 8GB GPU or potato specs .. \n\nHaving default settings targetted for lower end PCs is ok, but the end user should be able to increase the limits or they should be autocalculated based on the real PC VRChat is running on..",
      "viewerReactions": null,
      "voteID": null
    }
